# Not redundant with .gitignore. This is what stops a STALE LOCAL BUILD being copied into the
# image context, so what ships is always what the frontend stage just produced rather than
# whatever a developer last had on disk (notably an unoptimised `npm run watch` build).
src/api/Fireworks.Api/wwwroot/

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
**/.angular/
.git/
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/dist/
**/*.user
.env

# Team tooling, planning and reference material: never part of the image (plan Phase 1c).
.squad/
.claude/
plans/
docs/
prototypes/
# Local measuring kits (tools/fps-compare): run on a developer machine, never shipped.
tools/
# Shared schema fixtures and limits.json: test input only. CreationLimits.cs compiles the limits in
# and nothing at runtime reads schema/ (schema.md §6.6, Boo S29), so it stays out of the context.
schema/
